  "id": "The_Beginning_of_the_End_of_Social_Engineering_txt_23",
  "content": "Often, before suspicion is even activated, the email has already been opened, the link clicked, or the call answered because of habit and routine. From that point forward, attackers exploit engagement itself as a signal of vulnerability. This is why warning banners, phishing indicators, and countless other interventions have had only limited success. They arrive after the interaction has already begun.",
